=== intro

A docking bay manager flags you down—irritation clear in 
their signal patterns.

"You're Blackwing? Free trader? You travel a lot of routes."

Not a question.

"We're tracking Sera infestations. Need reports from 
traders who've seen activity. Station's paying for 
confirmed sightings."

* [What kind of sightings?]
  -> details

* [Not interested in pest control]
  ~ chronicle "Sera Sightings"
    Declined to report Sera sightings. Not getting involved in that headache.
  -> END

=== details

"Breeding colonies. Migration patterns. Which stations 
have contamination problems, which routes are heavy with 
spore drift."

The manager pulls up a map—trade routes marked with 
infestation reports.

"The damned things are spreading faster than usual this 
cycle. Every bit of data helps us stay ahead of them."

* [I've seen some activity]
  -> report

* [What's the pay?]
  -> pay

=== pay

"Twenty credits per confirmed sighting with coordinates. 
Fifty if you can tell us about a breeding colony location."

Standard pest-bounty rates. Not great, but steady work 
if you're traveling anyway.

* [I'll keep my sensors open]
  ~ credits += 10
  ~ flag sera_reporter
  ~ chronicle "Sera Sightings"
    Agreed to report Sera activity. Easy credits for information I'd gather anyway.
  -> END

* [Not worth the hassle]
  ~ chronicle "Sera Sightings"
    Pest control pay wasn't worth the record-keeping. Passed.
  -> END

=== report

"Good. Mark the coordinates here—we'll cross-reference 
with other reports."

You upload what you know. Spore drift near the third 
beacon. A station that had to vent two cargo bays last 
cycle. The usual trader gossip about infestations.

"This helps. Here's your payment. Flag us if you see 
more."

* [Will do]
  ~ credits += 35
  ~ flag sera_reporter
  ~ chronicle "Sera Sightings"
    Reported Sera activity to station management. Got paid for pest intelligence.
  -> END
